              "id": "1ffaf041-f880-39bd-824e-02b646635a73",
              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability\" in JavaScript refers to the security risk associated with sending sensitive data over an unencrypted HTTP connection. This can lead to the interception of data by malicious actors, who can then use this data for nefarious purposes. This vulnerability is particularly relevant when dealing with sensitive data such as login credentials, personal information, or financial data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when dealing with sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data sent between the client and the server, making it much more difficult for a third party to intercept and understand the data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code, there is no explicit usage of HTTP or HTTPS. However, the `ChatbotService` and `provideHttpClient` might be using HTTP under the hood. You should ensure that these services are configured to use HTTPS. The exact changes depend on the implementation of these services, but it might look something like this:\n\n```javascript\nTestBed.configureTestingModule({\n  imports: [],\n  providers: [\n    ChatbotService,\n    provideHttpClient(withInterceptorsFromDi(), { useHttps: true }),\n    provideHttpClientTesting({ useHttps: true })\n  ]\n})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to be using Angular's testing utilities, so the following dependencies are required:\n\n- `@angular/core`\n- `@angular/common/http`\n- `@angular/platform-browser-dynamic/testing`\n\nThe `ChatbotService` and `provideHttpClient` are not standard Angular services, so they might require additional dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10-2017 A6-Security Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A6_2017-Security_Misconfiguration)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-319",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-319"
                ]
              }
