            {
              "id": "abc808d8-f313-3cc8-8233-d9da5c857f3b",
              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability\" in JavaScript refers to the security risk associated with sending sensitive data over an unencrypted HTTP connection. This can lead to the interception of the data by malicious actors, leading to data breaches and other security issues. This vulnerability is particularly relevant when dealing with sensitive data such as login credentials, personal information, or financial data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when dealing with sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data between the client and the server, making it much more difficult for a third party to intercept and read the data.\n\nIn addition, it is also recommended to use HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) which is a web security policy mechanism that helps to protect websites against protocol downgrade attacks and cookie hijacking.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe provided code does not show the usage of HTTP or HTTPS, but generally, to fix this vulnerability, you should ensure that all HTTP requests are changed to HTTPS. If you are using a library like axios, you can set the base URL to use HTTPS like so:\n\n```javascript\naxios.defaults.baseURL = 'https://your-api-url.com';\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to be using Angular's testing utilities and seems to require the following dependencies:\n\n- `@angular/core`\n- `@angular/common/http`\n- `@angular/common/http/testing`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Transport Layer Protection Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Protection_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Unvalidated Redirects and Forwards Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Unvalidated_Redirects_and_Forwards_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n## CWE\n\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
