              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability\" in JavaScript refers to the security risk associated with sending sensitive data over unencrypted HTTP connections. This vulnerability can lead to exposure of sensitive data to unauthorized parties, as the data can be easily intercepted and read by anyone who has access to the network.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the TestBed is configuring a module with a DeliveryService and two HttpClient providers. If these services are communicating with a server over an unencrypted HTTP connection, any data sent or received could be at risk.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when dealing with sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data sent between the client and the server, making it much more difficult for unauthorized parties to intercept and read the data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific fix would depend on the implementation of the `provideHttpClient`, `withInterceptorsFromDi`, and `provideHttpClientTesting` functions, as well as the `DeliveryService` class. However, in general, you should ensure that these services are configured to use HTTPS. For example, if `provideHttpClient` is creating an instance of Angular's `HttpClient`, you could ensure that the base URL it's using is an HTTPS URL.\n\n```javascript\nTestBed.configureTestingModule({\n  imports: [],\n  providers: [DeliveryService, provideHttpClient(withInterceptorsFromDi('https://secure-url')), provideHttpClientTesting('https://secure-url')]\n})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet appears to be using Angular's TestBed, so the `@angular/core` and `@angular/common/http` packages would be required. The specific dependencies for `DeliveryService`, `provideHttpClient`, `withInterceptorsFromDi`, and `provideHttpClientTesting` would depend on their implementations.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP: Transport Layer Protection Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Protection_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
