            {
              "id": "2f7e7550-6f2a-3411-9603-bfa56d9a0cad",
              "name": "Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nA potential Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability can occur when user-controlled data is directly included in an HTML string without proper sanitization or encoding. In the provided JavaScript code, the product name, which could potentially be user-controlled data, is directly included in an HTML string. This could allow an attacker to inject malicious scripts, which would then be executed in the context of the victim's browser.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to always sanitize or encode user-controlled data before including it in an HTML string. Sanitization involves removing or replacing any potentially harmful characters, while encoding involves converting these characters into a safe format that the browser will not interpret as code.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code, you can mitigate the potential XSS vulnerability by encoding the product name before including it in the HTML string. Here's how you can do it:\n\n```javascript\nlet encodedProductName = encodeURIComponent(product.name);\nthis.snackBarHelperService.open(`Price for ${encodedProductName} has been updated.`, 'confirmBar');\n```\n\nIn this code, `encodeURIComponent` is a built-in JavaScript function that encodes special characters. In this case, it will encode any special characters in the product name, preventing them from being interpreted as code.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to be using a custom service `snackBarHelperService` to display a message. The exact library dependencies would depend on the implementation of this service and the overall project. However, it's likely that this code is part of an Angular application, which would require the `@angular/core` library.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Resources\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "612a49c3-705b-3306-99cb-b6c3c9a8a581",
              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability\" in JavaScript refers to the security risk associated with sending sensitive data over unencrypted HTTP connections. This can lead to data being intercepted, read, and modified by attackers. This vulnerability is particularly dangerous when dealing with sensitive data such as user credentials, personal information, or financial data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when dealing with sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data between the client and the server, making it much harder for attackers to intercept and read the data. \n\nIn addition, consider using HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS), which is a web security policy mechanism that helps to protect websites against protocol downgrade attacks and cookie hijacking.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code, the HTTP client is provided without specifying whether it should use HTTP or HTTPS. To fix this, you should ensure that all requests made by the HTTP client are sent over HTTPS. This can be done by configuring the HTTP client to use HTTPS by default.\n\n```javascript\nTestBed.configureTestingModule({\n  imports: [RouterTestingModule,\n    TranslateModule.forRoot(),\n    ReactiveFormsModule,\n    BrowserAnimationsModule,\n    MatCardModule,\n    MatFormFieldModule,\n    MatInputModule,\n    MatGridListModule,\n    MatIconModule,\n    MatSnackBarModule,\n    AddressCreateComponent],\n  providers: [\n    { provide: AddressService, useValue: addressService },\n    { provide: TranslateService, useValue: translateService },\n    { provide: MatSnackBar, useValue: snackBar },\n    provideHttpClient(withInterceptorsFromDi(), { useHttps: true }), // Ensure HTTPS is used\n    provideHttpClientTesting()\n  ]\n})\n  .compileComponents()\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `@angular/router/testing`\n- `@ngx-translate/core`\n- `@angular/forms`\n- `@angular/platform-browser/animations`\n- `@angular/material/card`\n- `@angular/material/form-field`\n- `@angular/material/input`\n- `@angular/material/grid-list`\n- `@angular/material/icon`\n- `@angular/material/snack-bar`\n- `AddressCreateComponent` (custom component)\n- `AddressService` (custom service)\n- `TranslateService` (custom service)\n- `MatSnackBar` (custom service)\n- `provideHttpClient` (custom function)\n- `provideHttpClientTesting` (custom function)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Transport Layer Protection Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Protection_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-319",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-319"
                ]
              }
