            {
              "id": "6f071deb-e5f2-3a28-b0af-cacbbf46bfa4",
              "name": "\"Vulnerability to Man-in-the-Middle Attacks due to Use of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Instead of HTTPS\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability \"Vulnerability to Man-in-the-Middle Attacks due to Use of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Instead of HTTPS\" refers to the risk of sensitive data being intercepted when it is transmitted over an unencrypted HTTP connection. In JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when the application communicates with the server using HTTP instead of HTTPS. A Man-in-the-Middle (MitM) attacker can intercept and potentially alter the communication between the client and the server.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS for all types of communication between the client and the server. HTTPS ensures that the data is encrypted and cannot be read by anyone who intercepts it. \n\nIn addition, consider implementing HTTP Strict Transport Security (HSTS) to ensure that the browser only communicates with the server using a secure HTTPS connection. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe TestBed configuration does not directly deal with HTTP or HTTPS. The actual HTTP requests are likely made in the services provided in the TestBed configuration. Therefore, you should ensure that these services always use HTTPS for their requests. \n\nFor example, if you are using Angular's HttpClient, make sure to use HTTPS in the URL:\n\n```javascript\nthis.http.get('https://example.com/api/data');\n```\n\nInstead of:\n\n```javascript\nthis.http.get('http://example.com/api/data');\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example seems to be using Angular's testing utilities. The following libraries are likely required:\n\n- `@angular/core`\n- `@angular/router`\n- `@angular/common/http`\n- `@angular/router/testing`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Transport Layer Protection Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Protection_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
