            {
              "id": "ec455e14-f8c2-35e4-8618-af62275de93b",
              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability\" in JavaScript refers to the security risk associated with sending sensitive data over unencrypted HTTP connections. This can lead to data being intercepted, read, and modified by attackers. In the context of the provided code, if the TestBed is configured to use an unencrypted HTTP server, any data sent or received could be vulnerable.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when dealing with sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data sent between the client and the server, making it much more difficult for attackers to intercept and read the data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe provided code does not directly show usage of HTTP or HTTPS. However, if it is using HTTP, you should switch to HTTPS. This is typically done in the configuration of the server or the API endpoints, not in the TestBed configuration. \n\nFor example, if you have an API endpoint like this:\n\n```javascript\nconst API_ENDPOINT = 'http://example.com/api';\n```\n\nYou should change it to use HTTPS:\n\n```javascript\nconst API_ENDPOINT = 'https://example.com/api';\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code appears to require the following libraries:\n\n- `@angular/core` for `TestBed`\n- `@angular/router/testing` for `RouterTestingModule`\n- `ErrorPageComponent`, `DeluxeGuard`, `LoginGuard`, `provideHttpClient`, `withInterceptorsFromDi`, and `provideHttpClientTesting` are not standard Angular libraries and may be custom components or services. You would need to include these in your project for the code to work.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10-2017 A6-Security Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A6_2017-Security_Misconfiguration)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
