            {
              "id": "78b9ec53-5be8-371c-ad92-1f4e66342225",
              "name": "\"Exclusion of Unreadable Files from Scans Due to High False Positive Rates\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability \"Exclusion of Unreadable Files from Scans Due to High False Positive Rates\" refers to a situation where certain files are excluded from security scans because they are unreadable or cause too many false positives. This can lead to potential security risks as these files may contain malicious code or other security vulnerabilities that are not detected.\n\nIn JavaScript programming, this vulnerability can occur when using various libraries and modules. If these libraries or modules have files that are unreadable or cause high false positive rates during security scans, they may be excluded from the scans, potentially leaving security vulnerabilities undetected.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Ensure that all files, regardless of their readability or false positive rates, are included in security scans. This can help detect any potential security vulnerabilities that may be present in these files.\n\n2. Use reliable and accurate security scanning tools. This can help reduce the number of false positives and improve the readability of files during scans.\n\n3. Regularly update and patch all libraries and modules used in your JavaScript programming. This can help fix any known security vulnerabilities and improve the overall security of your code.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nSince this vulnerability is more about the process of security scanning rather than specific code issues, there's no direct source code fix. However, ensuring your code is clean, well-documented, and follows best practices can help make security scanning more effective.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example provided requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- MatTable\n- MatColumnDef\n- MatHeaderCellDef\n- MatHeaderCell\n- MatCellDef\n- MatCell\n- MatRadioButton\n- MatIconButton\n- MatHeaderRowDef\n- MatHeaderRow\n- MatRowDef\n- MatRow\n- MatExpansionPanel\n- MatExpansionPanelHeader\n- MatExpansionPanelTitle\n- MatExpansionPanelDescription\n- MatFormFieldModule\n- MatLabel\n- TranslateModule\n- MatInputModule\n- FormsModule\n- ReactiveFormsModule\n- MatError\n- MatHint\n- MatButtonModule\n- MatIconModule\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [CWE for Security Features](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/693.html)\n\nPlease note that these links are subject to change and may not be available at all times. Always ensure to use the most up-to-date and reliable resources when dealing with security vulnerabilities."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL"
              }
