                    "id": "CWE-74",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/74.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-74"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "cd96b640-67a3-3b6d-91f1-120650591649",
              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe usage of unencrypted HTTP servers vulnerability in JavaScript refers to the risk of transmitting sensitive data over an unencrypted connection. This can lead to data being intercepted and manipulated by attackers. In the context of JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when making HTTP requests to an unencrypted server.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when transmitting sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data between the client and the server, making it much more difficult for attackers to intercept and read the data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code, there is no explicit usage of HTTP or HTTPS. However, if there is any HTTP request being made in the services or components, it should be replaced with HTTPS. For example, if there is a service making HTTP requests like this:\n\n```javascript\nthis.http.get('http://example.com/data');\n```\n\nIt should be replaced with:\n\n```javascript\nthis.http.get('https://example.com/data');\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- `@angular/core`\n- `@angular/forms`\n- `@angular/platform-browser/animations`\n- `@angular/material`\n- `@ngx-translate/core`\n- `ProductDetailsComponent`\n- `UserService`\n- `ProductReviewService`\n- `MatDialog`\n- `MAT_DIALOG_DATA`\n- `provideHttpClient`\n- `provideHttpClientTesting`\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
