            {
              "id": "0acdd56e-6b63-319b-a932-d31b52bcdce6",
              "name": "Usage of Unencrypted HTTP Servers Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe usage of unencrypted HTTP servers vulnerability in JavaScript refers to the risk of transmitting sensitive data over an unencrypted connection. This can lead to data being intercepted and manipulated by attackers. In the context of the provided code, if the `HttpClient` is used to make HTTP requests to an unencrypted server, it could expose sensitive user data or application data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use HTTPS (HTTP Secure) instead of HTTP when transmitting sensitive data. HTTPS encrypts the data between the client and the server, making it much harder for attackers to intercept and understand the data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific fix would depend on how the `HttpClient` is used in the rest of the application. However, as a general rule, ensure that all URLs used with the `HttpClient` start with `https://` instead of `http://`.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `@angular/core` for `TestBed`\n- `@ngx-translate/core` for `TranslateModule`\n- `ngx-cookie` for `CookieModule`\n- `@angular/material` for `MatIconModule` and `MatTooltipModule`\n- `@angular/common/http` for `HttpClient`\n- The `WelcomeBannerComponent`, `MatDialogRef`, `ConfigurationService`, and `CookieService` are likely custom components/services and would need to be imported from their respective files.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10-2017 A6-Security Misconfiguration](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A6_2017-Security_Misconfiguration)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-319",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
