              "id": "3f47bd87-992c-36f7-b7af-2beb2913a6d6",
              "name": "\"User-Controlled Data in 'd' Leads to XSS Vulnerabilities\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability \"User-Controlled Data in 'd' Leads to XSS Vulnerabilities\" in JavaScript refers to a situation where user-controlled data is directly used in the `innerHTML` property of an HTML element. This can lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities, as an attacker can inject malicious scripts into the web page, which are then executed in the context of the victim's session.\n\nIn the provided code, the `d.innerHTML=c;` line is vulnerable to XSS, as the variable `c` is directly controlled by the user.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid using user-controlled data directly in the `innerHTML` property. Instead, use `textContent` or `innerText` properties, which do not interpret the input as HTML, thus preventing script injection.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is the recommended fix for the provided code:\n\n```javascript\ndat.controllers.OptionController=function(e,a,b){var d=function(f,c,e){d.superclass.call(this,f,c);var k=this;this.__select=document.createElement(\"select\");if(b.isArray(e)){var l={};b.each(e,function(a){l[a]=a});e=l}b.each(e,function(a,c){var d=document.createElement(\"option\");d.textContent=c;d.setAttribute(\"value\",a);k.__select.appendChild(d)});this.updateDisplay();a.bind(this.__select,\"change\",function(){k.setValue(this.options[this.selectedIndex].value)});this.domElement.appendChild(this.__select)};\n```\n\nIn this fix, `d.innerHTML=c;` is replaced with `d.textContent=c;`.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to depend on a library similar to jQuery for the `b.each` and `a.bind` functions. However, without more context, it's hard to determine the exact library.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)\n\nPlease note that the links were active and accessible at the time of writing this report."
