            {
              "id": "fa296d68-ad40-3734-bc51-170d1da75421",
              "name": "\"XSS Vulnerability Risk in User-Controlled Data with `a.__preset_select[b]` Anti-Pattern\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability described here is a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability that occurs when user-controlled data is directly used to manipulate the `innerHTML` property of an HTML element. In the provided code, the `a.__preset_select[b].value` is directly assigned to `a.__preset_select[b].innerHTML` without any sanitization or encoding. If an attacker can control the value of `a.__preset_select[b].value`, they can inject malicious scripts that will be executed in the context of the victim's browser.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should never directly assign user-controlled data to the `innerHTML` property. Instead, use text nodes or properly encode the user input to ensure that any HTML special characters are treated as literal text rather than HTML markup.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the specific vulnerability sink:\n\n```javascript\ng.bind(q,\"change\",function(){\n  for(var b=0;b<a.__preset_select.length;b++){\n    var textNode = document.createTextNode(a.__preset_select[b].value);\n    while (a.__preset_select[b].firstChild) {\n      a.__preset_select[b].removeChild(a.__preset_select[b].firstChild);\n    }\n    a.__preset_select[b].appendChild(textNode);\n  }\n  a.preset=this.value\n});\n```\n\nIn this fix, we create a text node with the user-controlled data and append it to the element. This ensures that the user-controlled data is treated as literal text and not HTML markup.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example does not provide enough context to determine the library dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
