            {
              "id": "ae61029c-2fef-3440-bce6-4bcafc8c4882",
              "name": "\"User-Controlled Data Anti-Pattern Leading to XSS Vulnerabilities\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"User-Controlled Data Anti-Pattern Leading to XSS Vulnerabilities\" is a common security vulnerability in JavaScript programming. It occurs when user-controlled data is used directly in a security-sensitive operation without proper validation or sanitization. In this case, the user-controlled data is used to retrieve an item from the local storage. If an attacker can control the data, they can potentially inject malicious scripts leading to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to always validate and sanitize user-controlled data before using it in any security-sensitive operation. This includes:\n\n- Using built-in functions or libraries to sanitize user input.\n- Avoiding the use of user-controlled data in security-sensitive operations whenever possible.\n- Implementing proper error handling to prevent the execution of malicious scripts.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code, the vulnerability can be fixed by validating and sanitizing the user-controlled data before using it to retrieve an item from the local storage. Here is a simple fix:\n\n```javascript\nvar url = document.location.href;\nif (validateURL(url)) {\n    localStorage.getItem(url + \".isLocal\") && b.setAttribute(\"checked\", \"checked\");\n}\n```\n\nIn this fix, `validateURL(url)` is a function that validates the URL and returns `true` if it is valid and `false` otherwise. You need to implement this function according to your application's requirements.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code seems to be using a custom library `g` for event binding. No other library dependencies can be identified from the provided code.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)\n\nPlease note that the links are valid and active at the time of writing this report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
