            {
              "id": "5448ea89-e19f-3423-90cc-2ffe21caf913",
              "name": "Is prompt() call appropriate for production code?",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `prompt()` function is a part of JavaScript that allows you to create a dialog box which prompts the user for input. However, it is not recommended for use in production code due to several reasons. Firstly, it is synchronous, which means it halts the execution of the rest of the code until the user responds. Secondly, it is not customizable and does not match the look and feel of most websites. Lastly, it can be a potential security risk as it can be used for phishing attacks if not properly sanitized.\n\nThe provided code snippet uses the `prompt()` function to ask the user for a new preset name. This could potentially be exploited by an attacker to execute a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attack if the input is not properly sanitized before being used.\n\n## Mitigation\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid using the `prompt()` function in production code. Instead, use more modern and secure methods for getting user input, such as creating a custom dialog box using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. This not only improves the user experience but also allows for better input validation and sanitization.\n\n## Code Fix\n\nReplace the `prompt()` function with a custom dialog box. Here is an example of how you can do this:\n\n```javascript\nfunction(){a.save()});g.bind(e,\"click\",function(){\n    var b = window.confirm(\"Enter a new preset name.\");\n    if (b != null) {\n        a.saveAs(b);\n    }\n});g.bind(f,\"click\",function(){a.revert()})\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code seems to be using jQuery for event handling and DOM manipulation. Therefore, jQuery is a required library dependency for this code to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
