            {
              "id": "4df9762a-ec60-3f6d-abf4-4f5498e062e7",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability \"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\" refers to a situation where an application includes untrusted data in a new HTML string and sends it to a web browser without proper validation or escaping. This can allow an attacker to inject malicious scripts into the web page, which will be executed in the user's browser. This is known as a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attack.\n\nIn the provided JavaScript code, the potential vulnerability lies in the use of `document.createElement(\"div\")` and the subsequent manipulation of the created element's style properties. If any of these properties are controlled by user input, it could lead to an XSS vulnerability.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Avoid inserting user-controlled data into HTML strings.\n2. Use appropriate output encoding libraries to ensure that any user-controlled data is properly escaped before it is included in the HTML output.\n3. Use Content Security Policy (CSP) to reduce the severity of any XSS vulnerabilities.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nWithout knowing the full context of the code, it's hard to provide a specific fix. However, a general recommendation would be to ensure that any user-controlled data is properly validated and escaped before it is used. For example, if the `width` property is user-controlled, it should be validated to ensure it is a valid number and does not contain any malicious scripts.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code seems to be using a library `g` for event binding and `h` for extending objects. The exact libraries cannot be determined from the provided code snippet.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
