            {
              "id": "215d0403-506c-3d91-beeb-ea5a62c2249a",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe code snippet provided is vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. This is due to the use of user-controlled data in HTML strings without proper sanitization or encoding. An attacker can inject malicious scripts into the web page, which will then be executed in the browser of any user viewing that page. This can lead to a variety of attacks such as stealing user's cookies, performing actions on behalf of the user, or even delivering malware.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always encode user-controlled data before including it in an HTML string. This will prevent any potentially harmful scripts from being executed. Additionally, you should use secure methods for manipulating the DOM, such as `textContent` or `createTextNode`, instead of `innerHTML` or `style.cssText`.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code snippet:\n\n```javascript\ndat.controllers.ColorController = function(e, a, b, d, f) {\n    function c(a, b, d, c) {\n        a.style.background = \"\";\n        f.each(l, function(e) {\n            let safeB = encodeURIComponent(b);\n            let safeD = encodeURIComponent(d);\n            let safeC = encodeURIComponent(c);\n            a.style.cssText += \"background: \" + e + \"linear-gradient(\" + safeB + \", \" + safeD + \" 0%, \" + safeC + \" 100%); \"\n        })\n    }\n    function p(a) {\n        a.style.background = \"\";\n        a.style.cssText += \"background: -moz-linear-gradient(top,  #ff0000 0%, #ff00ff 17%, #0000ff 34%, #00ffff 50%, #00ff00 67%, #ffff00 84%, #ff0000 100%);\";\n        a.style.cssText += \"background: -webkit-linear-gradient(top,  #ff0000 0%,#ff00ff 17%,#0000ff 34%,#00ffff 50%,#00ff00 67%,#ffff00 84%,#ff0000 100%);\";\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIn this fix, we use the `encodeURIComponent` function to encode the user-controlled data before including it in the HTML string.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code snippet does not appear to have any explicit library dependencies.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Links\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
