            {
              "id": "aaf96d1b-6810-3a32-9bcf-ceac43f123b2",
              "name": "XSS Vulnerability due to Dynamic Input in innerHTML",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. XSS allows attackers to execute scripts in the victim's browser which can hijack user sessions, deface web sites, or redirect the user to malicious sites.\n\nIn the provided JavaScript code, the vulnerability lies in the use of `innerHTML` property. This property is used to get or set the HTML content of an element. If this property is used to add HTML to a page, a malicious user could inject a script into your page, leading to an XSS attack.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using `innerHTML` to add text to a page. Instead, use `textContent`, `innerText`, or `Element.createText` which automatically escape HTML tags and thus prevent XSS attacks. If you need to add HTML, make sure to sanitize it first to remove any potentially harmful scripts.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `innerHTML` usage with `textContent`:\n\n```javascript\ni.textContent=\"FPS\";a.appendChild(i);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code does not seem to require any specific library dependencies to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP DOM based XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/DOM_based_XSS_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
