            {
              "id": "8b7850c3-8996-3a37-8e40-b1dbd8c5f01f",
              "name": "XSS Vulnerability due to Dynamic Input in innerHTML",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. In this case, the vulnerability is due to dynamic input in `innerHTML`.\n\nThe `innerHTML` property can be a dangerous method to use, as it can lead to XSS vulnerabilities if not used properly. If user input is directly inserted into `innerHTML`, an attacker can inject scripts that can be executed, leading to various attacks such as cookie theft, keylogging, phishing, and identity theft.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to avoid using `innerHTML` with user-supplied input. Instead, use safer alternatives such as `textContent` or `innerText` which do not interpret the passed content as HTML, but instead insert it as raw text.\n\nIf you must use `innerHTML`, ensure that the data is properly sanitized and escaped to prevent the execution of potentially harmful scripts. This can be done using various libraries or functions designed for this purpose.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nReplace the `innerHTML` usage with `textContent`:\n\n```javascript\nk.id=\"msText\";\nk.style.cssText=\"color:#0f0;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9px;font-weight:bold;line-height:15px\";\nk.textContent=\"MS\";\nd.appendChild(k);\nvar e=document.createElement(\"div\");\ne.id=\"msGraph\";\ne.style.cssText=\"position:relative;width:74px;height:30px;background-color:#0f0\";\nfor(d.appendChild(e);74>e.children.length;)\n{\n    j=document.createElement(\"span\"),\n    j.style.cssText=\"width:1px;height:30px;float:left;background-color:#131\",\n    e.appendChild(j);\n}\nvar t=function(b){\n    s=b;\n    switch(s){\n        case 0:a.style.display=\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code does not appear to have any library dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
