            {
              "id": "ffe549d8-452b-31bb-80be-6186e462e307",
              "name": "Sensitive Data Exposure in API Response",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nSensitive Data Exposure in API Response is a vulnerability that occurs when an API unintentionally exposes sensitive information in its responses. This can happen when developers include sensitive data in the response body, headers, or other parts of the HTTP response. The exposed data can be anything from user credentials, personal information, proprietary business data, or any other data that should not be publicly accessible. This vulnerability can lead to serious data breaches if exploited by malicious actors.\n\nIn JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when using the `res.json()` function to send responses in Express.js applications. If sensitive data is included in the object passed to `res.json()`, it will be included in the API response.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, developers should:\n\n- Always validate and sanitize input data.\n- Implement proper access controls to ensure that only authorized users can access sensitive data.\n- Avoid including sensitive data in API responses unless absolutely necessary.\n- Encrypt sensitive data when it must be included in API responses.\n- Use secure communication protocols like HTTPS to protect data in transit.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code snippet, there is no sensitive data being exposed. However, if there was, the fix would involve removing the sensitive data from the response. For example, if the response included a user's password, the fix would be:\n\n```javascript\nres.json({\n  setup: true,\n  // password: user.password // Remove this line\n});\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- express\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP API Security Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-api-security/)\n- [OWASP Top 10-2017 A3-Sensitive Data Exposure](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A3_2017-Sensitive_Data_Exposure)\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)"
