              "id": "dd052a7b-552d-3004-8fa6-ee292e5e14fb",
              "name": "API Response Includes Sensitive User Data",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"API Response Includes Sensitive User Data\" is a security vulnerability that occurs when an API endpoint unintentionally exposes sensitive user data in its response. This can lead to unauthorized access to user data, identity theft, and other security breaches. In JavaScript, this can occur when sensitive data is included in the response object without proper checks or sanitization.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should:\n\n1. Always validate and sanitize input data.\n2. Limit the data that you send in your responses. Only send what is necessary.\n3. Implement proper access controls to ensure that users can only access data that they are authorized to see.\n4. Encrypt sensitive data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code snippet, it's not clear what `body.cid` represents. If it's sensitive data, it should not be included in the response. Here's a fixed version of the code:\n\n```javascript\nres.json({ orderNo: uniqueOrderNumber(), paymentDue: dateTwoWeeksFromNow() })\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example seems to be using Express.js, a popular web application framework for Node.js. The `res.json()` method is part of the Express.js API.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP API Security Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-api-security/)\n- [OWASP Data Validation](https://owasp.org/www-community/OWASP_Validation_Regex_Repository)\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)"
