            {
              "id": "e5844093-ec5e-3337-a70b-11549a0b5e90",
              "name": "Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability\" in JavaScript occurs when a promise is rejected but there is no error handling mechanism in place to catch and handle the error. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, including crashes, and can potentially expose sensitive information in error messages.\n\nIn the provided code, the promise returned by `BasketItemModel.findOne()` is not properly handled. If the promise is rejected, the application will throw an unhandled promise rejection error.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always include error handling for promises. This can be done by chaining a `.catch()` block to the promise, which will catch any errors that occur during the execution of the promise. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code:\n\n```javascript\nBasketItemModel.findOne({ where: { id: req.params.id } })\n  .then((item: BasketItemModel | null) => {\n    const user = security.authenticatedUsers.from(req)\n    challengeUtils.solveIf(challenges.basketManipulateChallenge, () => { return user && req.body.BasketId && user.bid != req.body.BasketId }) // eslint-disable-line eqeqeq\n    if (req.body.quantity) {\n      if (item == null) {\n        throw new Error('No such item found!')\n      }\n      void quantityCheck(req, res, next, item.ProductId, req.body.quantity)\n    } else {\n      next()\n    }\n  })\n  .catch((error: Error) => {\n    // Add error handling logic here\n    console.error(error);\n    res.status(500).send({ error: 'An error occurred' });\n  });\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- A promise-based ORM library (like Sequelize) for the `BasketItemModel.findOne()` function.\n- An Express.js or similar web framework for handling HTTP requests and responses (`req`, `res`, `next`).\n- A security library or module for handling user authentication (`security.authenticatedUsers.from(req)`).\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_security_cheat_sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
