              "id": "e04b087f-b299-36a2-87fd-d9cd635a50a4",
              "name": "XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nCross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerabilities occur when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. XSS allows attackers to execute scripts in the victim's browser which can hijack user sessions, deface web sites, or redirect the user to malicious sites.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the application is vulnerable to XSS because it's embedding user-controlled data (`user.id`) directly into the HTML string without proper sanitization or encoding.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate XSS vulnerabilities, you should:\n\n1. Use a safe API which avoids the use of the interpreter entirely or provides a parameterized interface.\n2. If a safe API is not available, make sure to escape special characters using the specific escape syntax for that interpreter.\n3. Positive (\"white list\") input validation is also recommended, but is not a complete defense as many applications require special characters in their input.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIn the provided code snippet, you can mitigate the XSS vulnerability by encoding the `user.id` before embedding it into the HTML string. Here's how you can do it:\n\n```javascript\nconst escape = require('escape-html');\n\nres.status(200).json({\n  action: 'response',\n  body: bot.greet(escape(`${user.id}`))\n});\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Express.js: A web application framework for Node.js.\n- escape-html: A Node.js module for escaping HTML strings.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP XSS](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/xss/)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
