            {
              "id": "d96f547f-ef9e-350a-9b59-5b0f9f7d5d07",
              "name": "Sensitive Data Exposure in API Response",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nSensitive Data Exposure in API Response is a vulnerability that occurs when an application does not adequately protect sensitive information from being disclosed in API responses. This can include information such as passwords, credit card numbers, health records, or any other data that should be kept private. In JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when using the `res.json()` function to send API responses without properly sanitizing or encrypting the data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should:\n\n- Always encrypt sensitive data in transit and at rest.\n- Use secure protocols such as HTTPS for data transmission.\n- Implement proper access controls to ensure that only authorized users can access sensitive data.\n- Sanitize and validate all input and output data.\n- Use secure coding practices and perform regular code reviews to identify and fix security vulnerabilities.\n\n## Code Fix Recommendation\n\nIf `response` contains sensitive data, you should sanitize or encrypt it before sending it in the API response. Here's an example of how you can do this:\n\n```javascript\nconst crypto = require('crypto');\n\nfunction encrypt(text) {\n  const cipher = crypto.createCipher('aes-256-cbc', 'encryptionKey');\n  let encrypted = cipher.update(text, 'utf8', 'hex');\n  encrypted += cipher.final('hex');\n  return encrypted;\n}\n\n// ...\n\napp.get('/api/data', (req, res) => {\n  // Fetch data (contains sensitive data)\n  let response = fetchData();\n\n  // Encrypt sensitive data\n  response.sensitiveData = encrypt(response.sensitiveData);\n\n  // Send response\n  res.json(response);\n});\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n- Express.js\n- Crypto (built-in Node.js module)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP API Security: Data Exposure](https://owasp.org/www-project-api-security/)\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)"
