              "id": "6d69e94e-f8c9-311f-9052-df1c141c37c1",
              "name": "'/' HTTP route in Express handles GET requests.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe given code is an Express.js route handler for the `'/'` route. It handles GET requests and is vulnerable to a potential Unauthorized Access vulnerability. The vulnerability arises from the fact that the code uses a token from the request cookies to identify the logged-in user. If an attacker can obtain a valid token, they can impersonate a user and gain unauthorized access to the system.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to use secure methods for user authentication and session management. Express.js has several middleware options for this, such as Passport.js, express-session, or cookie-session. These libraries provide secure user authentication and session management features.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix using the express-session middleware:\n\n```javascript\nconst session = require('express-session');\n\napp.use(session({\n  secret: 'your secret',\n  resave: false,\n  saveUninitialized: true,\n  cookie: { secure: true }\n}))\n\nrouter.get('/', async (req: Request, res: Response, next: NextFunction) => {\n  if (!req.session.user) {\n    next(new Error('Blocked illegal activity by ' + req.socket.remoteAddress))\n    return\n  }\n  const email = req.session.user.email\n\n  // rest of the code\n})\n```\n\nIn this code, `req.session.user` is used to store the logged-in user's information. The `express-session` middleware automatically manages the session cookies in a secure manner.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Express.js\n- Sequelize (for the `SecurityAnswerModel` and `SecurityQuestionModel` models)\n- A library for managing sessions (e.g., express-session, cookie-session)\n- A library for managing cookies (e.g., cookie-parser)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Session Management Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-285: Improper Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/285.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-285",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/285.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-285"
                ]
              }
