            {
              "id": "7bb09c78-6895-3227-b4a0-a3f2bf120f80",
              "name": "NoSQL Injection Vulnerability in findOne() Function Due to Untrusted User Input",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe code snippet above is vulnerable to NoSQL injection due to the use of untrusted user input in the `findOne()` function. This function is used to retrieve a single document from a MongoDB collection that matches a specified filter. If the filter is constructed using untrusted user input, an attacker can manipulate the query to retrieve unauthorized data, modify data, or even delete data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always validate, sanitize, and escape user input before using it in a database query. You should also use parameterized queries or prepared statements to ensure that user input is always treated as data, not as part of the query.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a fixed version of the code:\n\n```javascript\nconst email = loggedInUser.data.email\n\ntry {\n  const sanitizedEmail = sanitize(email); // Add this line to sanitize the user input\n  const answer = await SecurityAnswerModel.findOne({\n    include: [{\n      model: UserModel,\n      where: { email: sanitizedEmail } // Use the sanitized input here\n    }]\n  })\n  if (answer == null) {\n    throw new Error('No answer found!')\n  }\n  const question = await SecurityQuestionModel.findByPk(answer.SecurityQuestionId)\n  if (question == null) {\n    throw new Error('No question found!')\n  }\n\n  res.render('dataErasureForm', { userEmail: sanitizedEmail, securityQuestion: question.question }) // Use the sanitized input here\n} catch (error) {\n  next(error)\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Express.js for handling HTTP requests and responses\n- Sequelize for interacting with the database\n- Any library for sanitizing user input, such as the `validator` library\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-89",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-89"
                ]
              }
