            {
              "id": "d57aad65-db91-3f10-b8c9-adb8111e91b1",
              "name": "'/' HTTP route in Express handles post requests.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe vulnerability in this code lies in the handling of user input in the `req.body.layout` parameter. This parameter is used to construct a file path which is then used to render a response. An attacker could potentially manipulate this parameter to access files they should not be able to, leading to a Local File Inclusion (LFI) vulnerability. \n\nThe code attempts to mitigate this by checking if the file path includes certain forbidden strings ('ftp', 'ctf.key', 'encryptionkeys'), but this is not a robust solution as it can be easily bypassed. For example, an attacker could use a different case (e.g., 'FTP') or use a relative path to bypass the check.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using user input to construct file paths wherever possible. If it is necessary, you should use a whitelist of allowed paths rather than a blacklist of forbidden ones. You should also validate and sanitize the user input to ensure it does not contain any unexpected characters or sequences.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```javascript\n// Import the 'path' module\nconst path = require('path')\n\n// ...\n\nrouter.post('/', async (req, res, next) => {\n  // ...\n\n  if (req.body.layout) {\n    // Resolve and normalize the file path\n    const filePath = path.resolve(req.body.layout)\n\n    // Check if the file path is in the whitelist\n    const allowedPaths = ['/path/to/allowed/file1', '/path/to/allowed/file2']\n    if (allowedPaths.includes(filePath)) {\n      res.render('dataErasureResult', {\n        ...req.body\n      }, (error, html) => {\n        // ...\n      })\n    } else {\n      next(new Error('File access not allowed'))\n    }\n  } else {\n    res.render('dataErasureResult', {\n      ...req.body\n    })\n  }\n})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n- express\n- path\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
