            {
              "id": "ecb5d956-a0cd-39c7-8618-c4577f01fcfd",
              "name": "Potential NoSQL Injection from Unsanitized `req` Argument in `../data/mongodb` Statement",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nPotential NoSQL Injection from Unsanitized `req` Argument in `../data/mongodb` Statement vulnerability refers to a security flaw where an attacker can inject malicious NoSQL queries through the `req` argument. This is because the `req` argument is directly used in a MongoDB query without any sanitization or validation. This can lead to unauthorized data access, data corruption, or even data loss.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always validate and sanitize user inputs. Never trust user inputs blindly. Use a proper data validation library to validate user inputs against a set of rules. Also, use a proper sanitization library to sanitize user inputs to remove any potential harmful data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple fix for the vulnerability. You should validate and sanitize the `updatedEmail` before using it in a MongoDB query.\n\n```javascript\nconst validator = require('validator');\nconst sanitize = require('mongo-sanitize');\n\n// ...\n\nlet updatedEmail = req.body.email;\n\nif (!validator.isEmail(updatedEmail)) {\n    throw new Error('Invalid email');\n}\n\nupdatedEmail = sanitize(updatedEmail);\n\ndb.ordersCollection.find({ email: updatedEmail }).then((orders: Array<{\n\n// ...\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/943.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-943",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/943.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-943"
