            {
              "id": "b6e07483-6db5-36a1-aa83-548f301030ac",
              "name": "Unselected Field Database Query Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Unselected Field Database Query Vulnerability\" in JavaScript is a security flaw that occurs when a developer does not explicitly specify the fields to be returned in a database query. This can lead to the exposure of sensitive data. For instance, if a user object is queried and the password hash is not explicitly excluded, it could be returned in the query result and potentially exposed to an attacker.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, developers should always explicitly specify the fields to be returned in a database query. This is often referred to as \"projection\" in MongoDB. By doing this, developers can ensure that sensitive data is not inadvertently included in the query results.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is an example of how to fix the vulnerability in the provided code snippet:\n\n```javascript\ndb.reviewsCollection.find({ author: email }, { password: 0 }).then((reviews: Array<{}>) => {\n  // rest of the code\n});\n```\n\nIn this example, the `{ password: 0 }` argument is added to the `find` method to explicitly exclude the `password` field from the query results.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example provided seems to be using MongoDB, so the following library dependencies are required:\n\n- MongoDB: A NoSQL database.\n- Mongoose: An Object Data Modeling (ODM) library for MongoDB and Node.js.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top Ten](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)\n- [OWASP Proactive Controls](https://owasp.org/www-project-proactive-controls/)\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-200",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html"
                  }
                ],
