            {
              "id": "69bd0e7a-1379-3eac-af58-e923ed2d0ce8",
              "name": "NoSQL Injection Vulnerability in findOne() Function Due to Untrusted User Input",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"NoSQL Injection Vulnerability in findOne() Function Due to Untrusted User Input\" is a security vulnerability that occurs when an application uses untrusted user input in a NoSQL query. This can allow an attacker to manipulate the query, leading to unauthorized data access, data loss, or other security breaches.\n\nIn the provided JavaScript code, the `findOne()` function of the `CardModel` object is used with untrusted user input (`req.body.paymentId` and `req.body.UserId`). This can potentially lead to a NoSQL injection if the user input is not properly validated or sanitized.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n- Always validate user input: Ensure that user input matches expected patterns and values.\n- Use parameterized queries or prepared statements: These can help ensure that user input is not executed as part of the query.\n- Use a web application firewall (WAF): A WAF can help detect and block NoSQL injection attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code:\n\n```javascript\nconst paymentId = req.body.paymentId;\nconst userId = req.body.UserId;\n\nif (typeof paymentId !== 'string' || typeof userId !== 'string') {\n    // Handle error: invalid input\n}\n\nconst card = await CardModel.findOne({ where: { id: paymentId, UserId: userId } });\n```\n\nIn this fix, the user input is checked to ensure it is a string before it is used in the `findOne()` function. If the input is not a string, an error is handled.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Express.js: For handling HTTP requests and responses.\n- Sequelize: For interacting with the database.\n\n## OWASP and CWE Resources\n\n- [CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/943.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-943",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/943.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-943"
                ]
              }
