            {
              "id": "77e90292-e808-34df-8330-f325aed66345",
              "name": "\"Code Injection Vulnerability Detected\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Code Injection Vulnerability Detected\" is a security vulnerability that occurs when an attacker can inject and execute malicious code within your application. In JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when user input is used in the execution context without proper sanitization or validation. This can lead to serious security issues such as data theft, data corruption, and denial of service.\n\nIn the provided code, the vulnerability exists because the `data` variable, which is passed to the `libxml.parseXml` function, is not validated or sanitized before use. This means that if an attacker can control the value of `data`, they can potentially inject malicious code that will be executed in the context of your application.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always validate and sanitize user input before using it in your application. This can be done using various techniques such as input validation, output encoding, parameterized queries, and using secure APIs.\n\nIn addition, you should also use the principle of least privilege, which means that code should only have the permissions it needs to perform its task and no more. This can help to limit the potential damage if a code injection vulnerability is exploited.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nA potential fix for the provided code could be to validate and sanitize the `data` variable before passing it to the `libxml.parseXml` function. This could be done using a library such as DOMPurify.\n\n```javascript\nconst DOMPurify = require('dompurify');\nconst { JSDOM } = require('jsdom');\n\nconst window = new JSDOM('').window;\nconst purify = DOMPurify(window);\n\nconst sanitizedData = purify.sanitize(data);\n\nconst xmlDoc = vm.runInContext(`libxml.parseXml(${sanitizedData}, { noblanks: true, noent: true, nocdata: true })`, sandbox, { timeout: 2000 });\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code requires the following libraries to execute properly:\n\n- `vm`: This is a core Node.js module and does not need to be installed separately.\n- `libxml`: This can be installed using npm with the command `npm install libxmljs`.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Code Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-94",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-94"
                ]
              }
