            {
              "id": "33d240e3-0741-3e41-a0f0-a6ba423a905c",
              "name": "\"Code Injection Vulnerability Detected\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Code Injection Vulnerability Detected\" is a security vulnerability that occurs when an attacker can inject and execute malicious code within your application. In JavaScript, this vulnerability can be exploited by manipulating the input data that is processed by the `eval()`, `setTimeout()`, `setInterval()`, `Function()`, or `vm.runInContext()` functions. \n\nIn the provided code example, the `vm.runInContext()` function is used to execute a string of code in a specific context. If an attacker can control the `data` variable, they can inject malicious code that will be executed when the `vm.runInContext()` function is called.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using functions that can execute strings of code whenever possible. If you must use these functions, make sure to properly sanitize and validate all input data. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of using `vm.runInContext()`, you can use `JSON.parse()` and `JSON.stringify()` to safely parse and stringify the YAML data:\n\n```javascript\nconst yaml = require('js-yaml');\nlet dataObject = yaml.safeLoad(data);\nconst yamlString = JSON.stringify(dataObject);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `vm`: This is a core Node.js module, so you don't need to install it separately.\n- `js-yaml`: You can install this library using npm: `npm install js-yaml`.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Code Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Code_Injection)\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-94",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
