            {
              "id": "79cf2406-71b8-372a-aee2-10610d9b5690",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe code snippet provided is vulnerable to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks. XSS is a type of injection, in which malicious scripts are injected into otherwise benign and trusted websites. XSS attacks occur when an attacker uses a web application to send malicious code, generally in the form of a browser side script, to a different end user. \n\nIn this case, the vulnerability arises from the fact that user-controlled data (`req.body.caption` and `req.body.UserId`) is directly used in the creation of an HTML string (`record`). If an attacker can control the content of these variables, they can inject malicious scripts that will be executed when the HTML string is rendered in a browser.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always escape user-controlled data before using it in HTML strings. This can be done using built-in functions or libraries that are designed for this purpose. \n\nIn addition, you should also validate and sanitize user input to ensure that it does not contain any malicious code. This can be done using a whitelist approach, where only certain types of input are allowed, or a blacklist approach, where certain types of input are explicitly disallowed.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple fix using the `escape-html` library to escape user-controlled data:\n\n```javascript\nconst escape = require('escape-html');\n\nconst record = {\n  caption: escape(req.body.caption),\n  imagePath: 'assets/public/images/uploads/' + req.file?.filename,\n  UserId: escape(req.body.UserId)\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `escape-html`: This library is used to escape user-controlled data before using it in HTML strings.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP XSS (Cross Site Scripting) Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://owasp.org/www-community/xss-filter-evasion-cheatsheet)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
