            {
              "id": "9d5c2f69-ba92-3402-83d3-01ff3f498cf8",
              "name": "\"Secure Network Access Endowment: Fetch(x) Data Leak Vulnerability Check\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Secure Network Access Endowment: Fetch(x) Data Leak Vulnerability Check\" vulnerability in JavaScript refers to the potential for unauthorized access to sensitive data when using the Fetch API. This can occur if the URL or parameters used in the fetch request contain sensitive data, or if the response from the fetch request is not properly secured.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, developers should:\n\n1. Avoid including sensitive data in the URL or parameters of a fetch request. If it is necessary to include such data, it should be encrypted.\n2. Ensure that the server's response to a fetch request does not include sensitive data. If it is necessary to include such data, it should be encrypted.\n3. Use HTTPS for all fetch requests to ensure that the data is encrypted in transit.\n4. Implement proper error handling to prevent the exposure of sensitive information in error messages.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple example of how to implement these recommendations:\n\n```javascript\nconst url = new URL('https://example.com');\nconst params = {param1: 'value1', param2: 'value2'};\nObject.keys(params).forEach(key => url.searchParams.append(key, params[key]));\n\ntry {\n    const response = await fetch(url, {\n        method: 'POST',\n        headers: {\n            'Content-Type': 'application/json',\n            // Include any necessary security headers here\n        },\n        body: JSON.stringify({\n            // Include any necessary data here, ensuring it is properly encrypted\n        }),\n    });\n\n    if (!response.ok) {\n        throw new Error('Network response was not ok');\n    }\n\n    const data = await response.json();\n    // Handle the data here, ensuring it is properly decrypted\n} catch (error) {\n    console.error('There has been a problem with your fetch operation:', error);\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example does not require any additional library dependencies to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
