            {
              "id": "92b7915d-513f-35cb-a70a-37379a27ef6b",
              "name": "\"Exposure of Error Details Vulnerability\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nExposure of Error Details Vulnerability in JavaScript refers to the situation where an application provides too much information in error messages. This can potentially expose sensitive information or system details that could be used by an attacker to exploit the system. In the provided code, if an error occurs, the application might expose the number of solved challenges that have been restored, which could be sensitive information.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to handle errors properly and avoid exposing sensitive information in error messages. This can be achieved by implementing a global error handler that catches all errors and returns a generic error message to the user. Additionally, logging the error details on the server side can be useful for debugging purposes without exposing sensitive information to the user.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code:\n\n```javascript\ntry {\n  // Your code here\n  res.json({ data: ids.length + ' solved challenges have been restored.' })\n} catch (error) {\n  console.error(error); // Log the error details on the server side\n  res.json({ error: 'An error occurred.' }); // Return a generic error message to the user\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- Express.js: A web application framework for Node.js, used to create the `res` object and its `json` method.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 - A3:2017-Sensitive Data Exposure](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A3_2017-Sensitive_Data_Exposure)\n- [CWE-209: Information Exposure Through an Error Message](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/209.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
