            {
              "id": "4cc78329-642f-3663-889d-707f6debeaa5",
              "name": "Unfiltered Database Query Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnfiltered Database Query Vulnerability, also known as NoSQL Injection, is a type of security vulnerability that occurs when an application doesn't properly validate or escape input before using it in a database query. This can allow an attacker to manipulate the query, potentially leading to unauthorized data access, data corruption, or even data loss.\n\nIn the provided JavaScript code, the vulnerability exists because the `id` variable is directly concatenated into the database query without any validation or escaping. This means that if an attacker can control the value of `id`, they can potentially manipulate the query to return unauthorized data or perform other malicious actions.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always validate and escape user input before using it in a database query. This can often be done using built-in functions or libraries provided by your database or programming language.\n\nIn addition, consider using parameterized queries or prepared statements, which can automatically handle input validation and escaping for you. These can often provide a higher level of security than manually validating and escaping input.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere's how you might fix the vulnerability in the provided code:\n\n```javascript\ndb.reviewsCollection.find({ product: id }).then((reviews: Review[]) => {\n```\n\nIn this fixed code, we're using MongoDB's built-in query syntax to search for documents where the `product` field equals `id`. This syntax automatically handles input validation and escaping, preventing NoSQL injection attacks.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code appears to use the following library dependencies:\n\n- MongoDB or a similar NoSQL database library\n- A promise library, such as Bluebird or native ES6 promises\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-943: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Data Query Logic](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/943.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-943",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/943.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-943"
                ]
              }
