            {
              "id": "4801f666-fbff-39a6-aa6b-31286a19d69f",
              "name": "Sensitive Data Exposure in API Response",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nSensitive Data Exposure in API Response is a vulnerability that occurs when an application unintentionally exposes sensitive data in its responses. This can happen when an application does not properly protect sensitive data, such as credit card numbers, social security numbers, or user passwords. In JavaScript, this can occur when using APIs to send or receive data.\n\nIn the provided code snippet, the `res.json(utils.queryResultToJson(reviews))` line could potentially expose sensitive data if the `reviews` object contains any sensitive information. This is because the `res.json()` function will convert the `reviews` object into a JSON string and include it in the API response.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should ensure that sensitive data is not included in the `reviews` object. This can be done by filtering out sensitive data before converting the `reviews` object into a JSON string.\n\nYou should also consider implementing additional security measures, such as data encryption and access controls, to further protect sensitive data.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple example of how you can filter out sensitive data from the `reviews` object:\n\n```javascript\nreviews = reviews.map(review => {\n  const {password, ...safeReview} = review;\n  return safeReview;\n});\n\nres.json(utils.queryResultToJson(reviews));\n```\n\nIn this example, the `map()` function is used to create a new array of reviews where each review does not include the `password` property.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet does not specify any library dependencies. However, it is likely that it requires the `express` library for handling HTTP responses and a utility library or function for converting query results into JSON.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Top 10 2017: A3-Sensitive Data Exposure](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A3_2017-Sensitive_Data_Exposure)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-200: Information Exposure](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-200",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/200.html"
