            {
              "id": "ce006807-be2b-3c96-ae45-9b66d8421bbf",
              "name": "MongoDB $where Operator NoSQL JavaScript Injection Vulnerability from Untrusted User Input",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe MongoDB `$where` operator is a powerful tool that allows developers to execute JavaScript code directly on the MongoDB server. However, if not used carefully, it can lead to NoSQL JavaScript Injection vulnerabilities. This happens when untrusted user input is directly used in a `$where` clause without proper sanitization or validation. An attacker can inject malicious JavaScript code, which will be executed on the MongoDB server, potentially leading to data leakage, data corruption, or even server takeover.\n\nIn the provided code, the `id` parameter is directly used in a `$where` clause without proper sanitization or validation, making it vulnerable to NoSQL JavaScript Injection.\n\n## Mitigation\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, avoid using the `$where` operator if possible. If you must use it, ensure that all user input is properly sanitized and validated before use. Use parameterized queries or prepared statements to prevent injection attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix\n\nReplace the `$where` operator with a safer alternative, like the `$eq` operator:\n\n```javascript\ndb.ordersCollection.find({ orderId: { $eq: id } }).then((order: any) => {\n  // ...\n})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- A MongoDB driver for Node.js, such as `mongodb` or `mongoose`\n- A utility library, such as `lodash` or `underscore`\n- An Express.js server\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-94: Improper Control of Generation of Code ('Code Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-94",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/94.html"
