            {
              "id": "f18929a8-ef7d-3bb5-8683-cbc8298e4a2f",
              "name": "\"Insecure Default Cookie Settings Lacking Critical Security Attributes: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Insecure Default Cookie Settings Lacking Critical Security Attributes: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite\" is a vulnerability that occurs when a web application does not properly set the security attributes of cookies. This can lead to various security issues such as Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks, Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks, and cookie theft.\n\nIn JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when using the `res.cookie()` function from the Express.js library without setting the `httpOnly`, `secure`, and `sameSite` attributes.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always set the `httpOnly`, `secure`, and `sameSite` attributes when creating cookies. \n\n- `httpOnly`: This attribute prevents the cookie from being accessed by client-side scripts, mitigating the risk of XSS attacks.\n- `secure`: This attribute ensures that the cookie is only sent over HTTPS, preventing the cookie from being intercepted during transmission.\n- `sameSite`: This attribute prevents the cookie from being sent with cross-site requests, mitigating the risk of CSRF attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is how you can fix the vulnerability in the provided code:\n\n```javascript\nres.cookie('token', updatedToken, { httpOnly: true, secure: true, sameSite: 'strict' });\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library to execute properly:\n\n- Express.js\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Secure Flags](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html#secure-attribute)\n- [OWASP - HttpOnly](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html#httponly-attribute)\n- [OWASP - SameSite](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html#samesite-attribute)\n- [CWE-1004: Sensitive Cookie Without 'HttpOnly' Flag](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1004.html)\n- [CWE-614: Sensitive Cookie Without 'Secure' Flag](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/614.html)\n- [CWE-319: Cleartext Transmission of Sensitive Information](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-1004",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/1004.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-614",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/614.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-319",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/319.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-1004",
                  "CWE-614",
                  "CWE-319"
                ]
              }
