            {
              "id": "1a3bbc5e-7c03-3592-afda-e9d15bebb8b7",
              "name": "Potential Session Fixation and Cross-Site-Scripting (XSS) Vulnerability due to User-Controlled Cookie Values",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nPotential Session Fixation and Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) Vulnerability due to User-Controlled Cookie Values is a security vulnerability that occurs when an application allows a user to control the value of a cookie without proper validation and sanitization. This can lead to session fixation attacks where an attacker can hijack a user's session. It can also lead to Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attacks where an attacker can inject malicious scripts into web pages viewed by other users.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to:\n\n1. Never trust user input: Always validate and sanitize user input before using it.\n2. Use HttpOnly cookies: This prevents the cookie from being accessed via JavaScript, mitigating the risk of XSS attacks.\n3. Use secure cookies: This ensures that the cookie is only sent over HTTPS, preventing it from being intercepted.\n4. Implement proper session management: This includes regenerating session IDs after login and logout, and implementing session timeouts.\n\n## Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```javascript\nconst express = require('express');\nconst cookieParser = require('cookie-parser');\nconst sanitize = require('validator').sanitize;\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use(cookieParser());\n\napp.get('/', (req, res) => {\n  let updatedToken = sanitize(req.cookies.token);\n  res.cookie('token', updatedToken, { httpOnly: true, secure: true });\n  res.send('Cookie is set');\n});\n\napp.listen(3000);\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n- Express.js\n- cookie-parser\n- validator\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Session Management Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Session_Management_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-384: Session Fixation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/384.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-384",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/384.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-384",
                  "CWE-79"
