              "id": "99c3520a-f497-3fbc-a198-93916f871f24",
              "name": "Unhandled Promise Rejections Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnhandled Promise Rejections Vulnerability in JavaScript occurs when a promise is rejected, but there is no error handling mechanism in place to catch and handle the error. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, including crashes and potential security vulnerabilities. In the provided code, the promise returned by `ComplaintModel.findAndCountAll()` is not properly handled in case of a rejection.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always ensure that promises have a `.catch()` method to handle any errors that may occur. This will prevent the application from crashing and provide a way to handle the error gracefully.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a recommended fix for the provided code:\n\n```javascript\nComplaintModel.findAndCountAll({\n    where: {\n      message: {\n        [Op.or]: weirdCryptos()\n      }\n    }\n  }).then(({ count }: { count: number }) => {\n    if (count > 0) {\n      challengeUtils.solve(challenges.weirdCryptoChallenge)\n    }\n  }).catch((error) => {\n    console.error('An error occurred:', error);\n  });\n```\n\nIn this fix, a `.catch()` method is added to the promise chain. If an error occurs, it will be logged to the console.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Sequelize (for `findAndCountAll` method and `Op.or` operator)\n- A library or module that provides `weirdCryptos`, `challengeUtils`, and `challenges` (not specified in the provided code)\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_security_cheat_sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
