              "id": "cc988626-aef4-3887-9db0-e21e40c41c30",
              "name": "Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nUnhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability in JavaScript occurs when a promise is rejected, but there is no error handling mechanism in place to catch and handle the error. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, including crashes, and can potentially expose sensitive information in error messages.\n\nIn the provided code, the promise returned by `FeedbackModel.findAndCountAll()` is not properly handled in case of rejection. If the promise is rejected, the error will be unhandled, which can lead to unexpected application behavior.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always include error handling for promises. This can be done by chaining a `.catch()` method to the promise, which will be called in case the promise is rejected. The `.catch()` method should include appropriate error handling logic.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```javascript\nFeedbackModel.findAndCountAll({ where: { comment: { [Op.like]: '%pickle rick%' } } }\n).then(({ count }: { count: number }) => {\n  if (count > 0) {\n    challengeUtils.solve(challenges.hiddenImageChallenge)\n  }\n}).catch((error) => {\n  console.error('An error occurred:', error);\n});\n```\n\nIn this fixed code, a `.catch()` method is added to handle any errors that may occur when the promise is rejected. The error is logged to the console, but in a real-world application, more sophisticated error handling should be implemented.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Sequelize (for the `findAndCountAll` method and `Op.like` operator)\n- A library or module that provides `challengeUtils` and `challenges`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
              },
