              "id": "40679154-b24e-3d41-93ce-a92de8175dec",
              "name": "Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability\" in JavaScript occurs when a Promise is rejected, but this rejection is not caught or handled. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, including crashes, and can potentially expose sensitive information or lead to other security vulnerabilities.\n\nIn the provided code, the Promise returned by `ComplaintModel.findAndCountAll()` is rejected, but the rejection is not handled in the `catch()` block. This can lead to an Unhandled Promise Rejection.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always handle Promise rejections. This can be done by providing a `.catch()` block after the Promise, or by using `try/catch` with async/await. In the `catch()` block, handle the error appropriately based on your application's needs. This might include logging the error, returning a default value, or re-throwing the error after logging it.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n```javascript\nComplaintModel.findAndCountAll({\n    where: {\n      message: { [Op.and]: dangerousIngredients() }\n    }\n  }).then(({ count }: { count: number }) => {\n    if (count > 0) {\n      challengeUtils.solve(challenges.dlpPastebinDataLeakChallenge)\n    }\n  }).catch((error) => {\n    console.error('An error occurred:', error);\n  });\n```\n\nIn this fix, the `catch()` block now logs the error to the console. This is a simple example; in a real application, you would likely want to do more sophisticated error handling.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code appears to require the following libraries:\n\n- Sequelize (for `findAndCountAll()`, `where`, and `Op`)\n- A library or module that provides `dangerousIngredients()`, `challengeUtils`, and `challenges`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
