              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\n\"Unhandled Promise Rejection Vulnerability\" is a common issue in JavaScript programming, particularly in Node.js applications. This vulnerability occurs when a promise is rejected, but there is no error handling mechanism in place to catch and handle the rejection. This can lead to unexpected application behavior, including crashes, and can potentially expose sensitive information or allow for other security vulnerabilities to be exploited.\n\nIn the provided code, the promise returned by `FeedbackModel.findAndCountAll()` is not properly handled in case of rejection. If the promise is rejected for any reason (for example, if there is a problem with the database connection), the application will crash or behave unexpectedly.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should always handle promise rejections. This can be done by adding a `.catch()` block to your promises, or by using `try/catch` with `async/await`. \n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a fixed version of your code:\n\n```javascript\nFeedbackModel.findAndCountAll({ where: { comment: { [Op.like]: '%6PPi37DBxP4lDwlriuaxP15HaDJpsUXY5TspVmie%' } } }\n  ).then(({ count }: { count: number }) => {\n    if (count > 0) {\n      challengeUtils.solve(challenges.leakedApiKeyChallenge)\n    }\n  }).catch((error) => {\n    console.error('An error occurred:', error);\n  });\n```\n\nIn this version, if the promise is rejected, the error will be logged to the console instead of crashing the application.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Sequelize (for the `findAndCountAll` function and `Op.like` operator)\n- A library or module that provides `challengeUtils` and `challenges`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Unhandled Promise Rejection](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Nodejs_Security_Cheat_Sheet.html#unhandled-promise-rejections)\n- [CWE-754: Improper Check for Unusual or Exceptional Conditions](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/754.html)"
