            {
              "id": "5f87cb71-f754-3626-a08f-a6074f1a6562",
              "name": "Detected Insecure Deserialization Vulnerability",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nInsecure Deserialization is a vulnerability that occurs when untrusted data is deserialized by a program. Since serialized data can be altered and then deserialized, this can lead to harmful effects such as code execution, denial of service, or bypassing security checks. In JavaScript, this vulnerability can occur when using functions like `yaml.load()` to deserialize untrusted data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid deserializing data from untrusted sources. If this is not possible, you should use safe deserialization functions that do not allow the execution of arbitrary code. You should also validate and sanitize the input data before deserializing it.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of using `yaml.load()`, you can use `yaml.safeLoad()`, which is a safe function that does not allow the execution of arbitrary code. Here is how you can fix the code:\n\n```javascript\nconst yaml = require('js-yaml');\nconst fs = require('fs');\n\nconst codingChallengeInfos = yaml.safeLoad(fs.readFileSync('./data/static/codefixes/' + key + '.info.yml', 'utf8'));\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- `js-yaml`: A JavaScript library for working with YAML, a human-friendly data serialization standard.\n- `fs`: A built-in Node.js module for working with the file system.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Insecure Deserialization](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A8_2017-Insecure_Deserialization)\n- [CWE-502: Deserialization of Untrusted Data](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-502",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/502.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-502"
                ]
              }
